From: Zac Bowling <zac@zacbowling.com>
Subject: [PATCH v6 00/13] wifi: mt76: mt7925: stability fixes for deadlocks, NULL derefs, and race conditions

This series addresses critical stability issues in the MT7925 WiFi driver
that cause kernel panics, deadlocks, and system hangs on Framework Desktop
systems and other hardware using the MT7925 WiFi card.

This v6 series is rebased on Sean Wang's upstream deadlock fix [1] which is
now included as patch 01/13. The remaining 12 patches are my stability fixes
reorganized for cleaner upstream review.

Changes since v5:
- Rebased on Sean Wang's fix for mt7925_roc_abort_sync deadlock (now patch 1)
- Fixed format string warning in patch 12: %lu -> %u for jiffies_to_msecs()
  return type (caught by kernel test robot)
- Added patch 13: fix double wcid initialization race condition - removes
  duplicate mt76_wcid_init() call that occurred after rcu_assign_pointer(),
  which could cause list corruption, memory leaks, and race conditions
  (this is a pre-existing bug in upstream, not introduced by this series)

Summary of the 13 patches:

Patch 01: Sean Wang's fix for ROC abort deadlock (upstream)
  Fixes cancel_work_sync() deadlock when called with mutex held.

Patch 02: mt76 core - fix list corruption in mt76_wcid_cleanup
  Prevents sta_poll_list corruption after device reset by using
  list_del_init() instead of list_del().

Patch 03: mt792x shared - fix NULL pointer and firmware reload issues
  Fixes NULL deref in TX path and firmware reload failure after crash.

Patches 04-05: mt7921 mutex and deadlock fixes
  Adds mutex protection and fixes deadlocks in sta removal paths.
  MT7921 shares code paths with MT7925.

Patches 06-09: mt7925 safety improvements
  - Comprehensive NULL pointer protection for MLO state transitions
  - Mutex protection in reset, ROC abort, runtime PM, and resume paths
  - MCU command error handling for AMPDU, BSS info, and key setup
  - Lockdep assertions for debugging mutex violations

Patches 10-11: mt7925 MLO and BA session fixes
  - Key removal and ROC setup fixes during MLO roaming
  - BA session teardown callback fix during beacon loss

Patch 12: mt7925 ROC deadlock and race condition fixes
  Comprehensive fix for ROC handling: deadlock in sta removal, timer race
  during suspend, rate limiting for MLO auth, WCID leak, and async abort
  race condition.

Patch 13: mt7925 double wcid initialization race fix
  Removes duplicate mt76_wcid_init() after RCU publish that could corrupt
  list heads and cause memory leaks.

Testing:
Tested extensively on Framework Desktop (AMD Ryzen AI Max 300 Series) with
MT7925 (RZ717) WiFi card. System is now stable through suspend/resume cycles,
MLO roaming, network switching, and firmware recovery scenarios that
previously caused crashes or hangs.

[1] https://lore.kernel.org/linux-wireless/sean.wang@mediatek.com

